Radix's terminals take Linux's TCGETS and TCSETS through
golang.org/x/sys/unix (term_nosyscall6.go); the files that call the
kernel through syscall.Syscall6 are not for Radix, where it fails.

diff -ruN a/github.com_chzyer_readline@v1.5.1/term.go b/github.com_chzyer_readline@v1.5.1/term.go
--- a/github.com_chzyer_readline@v1.5.1/term.go
+++ b/github.com_chzyer_readline@v1.5.1/term.go
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 // Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style
 // license that can be found in the LICENSE file.
 
-// +build aix darwin dragonfly freebsd linux,!appengine netbsd openbsd os400 solaris
+// +build aix darwin dragonfly freebsd linux,!appengine netbsd openbsd os400 radix solaris
 
 // Package terminal provides support functions for dealing with terminals, as
 // commonly found on UNIX systems.
diff -ruN a/github.com_chzyer_readline@v1.5.1/term_nosyscall6.go b/github.com_chzyer_readline@v1.5.1/term_nosyscall6.go
--- a/github.com_chzyer_readline@v1.5.1/term_nosyscall6.go
+++ b/github.com_chzyer_readline@v1.5.1/term_nosyscall6.go
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 // Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style
 // license that can be found in the LICENSE file.
 
